---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { sectorMap, patentProvenance, formatCount } from '../lib/data';
---

<Base
  title="Jack Kelly — Data governance and applied AI"
  description="A portfolio demonstrating data governance, judgment, and the encoding work that makes AI tools reliable, built on real USPTO patent data."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Data governance · Analytics · Applied AI</p>
  <h1>Turning messy public data into something a business can act on.</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    Two projects built on real USPTO patent data. The first asks which companies a law
    firm's IP practice should call, and shows its reasoning. The second is the governed
    layer that lets an AI tool answer questions about that data without inventing things.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout-limit">
    <span class="callout-label">What this is meant to demonstrate</span>
    <p style="margin-bottom:0">
      Charts are not the point. The point is judgment about which problems are worth
      solving, the governance work that makes a dataset trustworthy, and the encoding
      step that turns domain understanding into something a machine can execute against.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>The projects</h2>

  <div class="card-grid">
    <article class="card">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem">Project One</p>
      <h3><a href="/targeting">Business Development Targeting Engine</a></h3>
      <p>
        Which companies show the strongest signals of near-term demand for IP legal
        services? A transparent score, adjustable weights, and every rank decomposable
        into the components that produced it.
      </p>
      <p>
        {
          sectorMap
            ? `Practice-area sector mapping complete: ${sectorMap.subclasses_mapped} CPC subclasses across ${Object.keys(sectorMap.sectors).length} sectors, each validated against CPC edition ${sectorMap.cpc_edition}.`
            : 'Sector mapping not yet built.'
        }
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem">Project Two</p>
      <h3><a href="/semantic-layer">Governed Semantic Layer</a></h3>
      <p>
        The layer is the artifact, not the chat box. Documented entities, metrics with
        explicit formulas, allowed joins — and deliberate refusal when a question falls
        outside what the data can honestly answer.
      </p>
      <p>Layer definition in progress.</p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <h2>Ground rules</h2>

  <p>
    These constrain everything here, and they are worth stating before any finding is.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Every number is real and traceable.</strong> No synthetic data, no
      illustrative placeholders. Each figure traces to a specific file or API call, and
      the page says where it came from and when it was pulled.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The model's limits are on the page, not in a footnote.</strong> Patent
      activity is a proxy for legal services demand, and a flawed one. Where it breaks
      down is stated next to the results it produces.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The AI did not do the thinking.</strong> The semantic layer demo shows a
      model executing against a governed dataset using context that was authored by
      hand. The encoding is the work.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Current status</h2>

  <p>
    This is being built in phases and is not finished. Rather than fill the gaps with
    plausible-looking numbers, unfinished sections say what is missing.
  </p>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Phase</th>
          <th scope="col">State</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Pipeline foundation and provenance records</td>
          <td><span class="pill pill-live">Built</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>CPC to practice-area sector mapping</td>
          <td>
            {
              sectorMap ? (
                <span class="pill pill-live">Validated</span>
              ) : (
                <span class="pill pill-pending">Pending</span>
              )
            }
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>USPTO patent tables acquired</td>
          <td>
            {
              patentProvenance ? (
                <span class="pill pill-live">
                  {formatCount(
                    patentProvenance.files.flatMap((f) => f.tables).reduce((a, t) => a + (t.record_count ?? 0), 0)
                  )}{' '}
                  records
                </span>
              ) : (
                <span class="pill pill-pending">Awaiting download</span>
              )
            }
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Assignee normalization and data quality report</td>
          <td><span class="pill pill-pending">Blocked on data</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Scoring model</td>
          <td><span class="pill pill-pending">Blocked on data</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Semantic layer and refusal behavior</td>
          <td><span class="pill pill-pending">Blocked on data</span></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</Base>
